  "metaDescription": "Authorities are using DNA testing to identify victims of the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory fire in Cikande, Serang, as search efforts continue.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Authorities are collecting DNA samples and ante mortem data from families to identify victims recovered from the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia fire.",
    "Search and rescue teams have recovered 24 body bags, while 32 employees remain reported as missing following the blaze.",
    "Official investigations into the cause suggest the fire may have originated from a short circuit in an air conditioning unit."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "A major fire occurred at the PT Fonusa Agung Mulia candy factory located in Cikande, Serang, Banten, leading to a large-scale emergency response. Reports indicate that 29 individuals survived the incident, while 32 employees remain missing. Emergency services have evacuated 24 body bags from the scene, with authorities suggesting many victims may have been trapped on the second floor of the facility. To facilitate the identification process, 33 families have submitted ante mortem data. Government officials, including the Presidential Special Advisor for Manpower and Labor Welfare, have visited the site to oversee the response and emphasize corporate responsibility. Legislative members have also called for stricter enforcement of occupational health and safety standards within industrial areas to prevent future occurrences. The ongoing investigation into the fire’s origins currently points toward a potential electrical short circuit in an air conditioning unit as the primary cause.",
